meta {
  name: Get Email Code
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/email/code
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-Api-Key: {{emailCodeApiKey}}
}

docs {
  `GET /api/email/code`

  Loads the `EmailCodeEntity` from DynamoDB. Requires the `X-Api-Key` header.

  | Header      | Required | Notes                                         |
  | ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |
  | `X-Api-Key` | yes      | Must equal the API's `EmailCode:ApiKey` value |

  Set `emailCodeApiKey` as a secret in the Bruno environment - it is never
  written to the `.bru` files. Locally, give the API a key with
  `dotnet user-secrets set EmailCode:ApiKey <key> --project weather-backend`;
  in production it comes from the `EMAIL_CODE_API_KEY` GitHub Actions secret.

  No status assert: the result depends on that secret being set, and the API
  answers `503` when it has no key configured.
}
